the network performance tool allows the administrator to test and measure the latency and throughput of the network between delphix cde and environments. 

The Network Performance Tool is accessed by clicking the Resources Tab located on the Delphix Continuous Data Engine banner, and selecting Network Performance Tool.

options in Network Performance Tool Testing tab: 

    1. Latency 
    2. Throughput
    3. Delphix Session Protocol -- DSP


Network Latency:
    The Network Latency test measure the network roundup latency by transmitting the ICMP ECHO REQUEST and the time to recieve the replies from the remote host

    ICMP ECHO REQUEST: 
        An ICMP Echo Request (Type 8, Code 0) is a network-layer diagnostic message sent to test whether another device is reachable and online on an IP network
    
    can be accessed by - clicking on Latency in testing of NETWORK PERFORMANCE TOOL

NETWORK THROUGHPUT:
    This test supports two directions: Transmit and Receive. 

    Transmit: the Delphix Engine sends traffic and the remote host receives.

    Receive: the remote host sends traffic and the Delphix Engine receives.

    accessed by - clicking THROUGHPUT in Testing

Delphix Session Protocol(DSP):
    DSP test measure the dsp performance :
    * between 2 delphix CDE 
    * between a Delphix CDE and a source/target envi

Selecting an Environment

    For either a Latency or Throughput test, you must select an environment. If you selected an environment in the Datasets panel, this field will auto-populate. 

    For the DSP test, you have the option to test an engine or an environment, which gives you the option to test the default environment listed or select a different one.

The History Tab:
     this is next to testing tab
    In the History tab, you can view the results of all previous tests you have run by selecting the radio button for the type of test for which you want to see the results. 

    to see the details of any particular test, select the history tab and then click the test for which you want to see the results. 

